# tmp/ is a symlink into RAM -- /tmp for anything executable, /dev/shm for
# artifacts and logs. Nothing under it is the record, and the link itself points
# at a machine-local path, so the run scripts recreate it rather than the
# repository carrying it.
tmp

# output/ is where the last tool to finish left its goodbye. It is a mailbox
# rather than a record: overwritten every run, and meaningless to anyone who was
# not there when it was written. Keep the room, discard the letters.
output/*
!output/.gitkeep

# docs/HTML/ is the documentation site, and it is built rather than written.
# Every page in it is derived from a file already in this repository, and the
# whole tree rewrites whenever any dimension changes -- so tracking it would put
# the same words in the record twice and make a one-line edit to a blueprint
# look like two hundred changed files. The builder is the artifact.
#
#   luajit src/099-the-documentation-site.lua
docs/HTML/

# What the checker leaves behind. The pass/fail state of every constraint in the
# design is recomputed from the blueprints in under a second; a committed copy
# would be a second source of truth, and the second source is always the one
# that is wrong.
*.report
*.log

# Editor and platform litter.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
